{#
  text.twig — typographic helpers for body copy.
#}

{#
  standfirst(text)

  A plain-text summary rendered as one paragraph's worth of HTML: line breaks kept as
  <br>, and the LAST TWO WORDS OF EVERY LINE made unbreakable, so a line can never end
  on a word by itself.

  ── WHY NOT `text-wrap: pretty` ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Because SAFARI DOES NOT IMPLEMENT IT. Measured 2026-09-15 via tools/safari:
  `CSS.supports('text-wrap','pretty')` is false in Safari, true in Chrome. Safari also
  measures this mono a shade tighter and fits one more word on the line above, so
  /ai-policy renders as

      Chrome:  "Every design on this website is my" / "own work."
      Safari:  "Every design on this website is my own" / "work."     <- orphan

  at every width from 1024 up. Sweeping all 52 pages in CHROME reports no orphan
  anywhere on the site; the same sweep in Safari finds them immediately. TEST WRAPPING
  IN SAFARI. The guarantee therefore lives in the markup, where every browser honours
  it, not in a property one of them ignores.

  ── WHY NOT `text-wrap: balance` ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  It works, and it was tried and reverted: balance re-flows EVERY line of the
  paragraph to even them up, which is a whole-paragraph change to stop one word being
  lonely. This moves one word and leaves every other break where the browser put it.

  ── WHY NOT Craft's own `|widont` ────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Craft ships one (Html::widont) and it is one regex: `&nbsp;` before the last word.
  It misses both things that actually matter below — the hyphen and the cap — and it
  is registered `is_safe => html`, so `{{ summary|widont }}` marks the WHOLE string
  safe and silently stops Twig escaping a plain-text CMS field.

  ── WHY NOT a `white-space: nowrap` span ─────────────────────────────────────────
  Tried, measured, reverted. In Safari an inline nowrap run at the end of a paragraph
  makes the line REFUSE TO BREAK AT ALL rather than move the run down: /ai-policy at
  1440 went to a single line 750px wide in a 740px column — 10px hanging out of the
  measure — where the same text as plain characters wrapped to two lines cleanly.
  Invisible characters do not have that effect.

  ── WHAT IT ACTUALLY DOES ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  1. A NON-BREAKING SPACE joins the last two words, removing the break between them.
  2. A WORD JOINER (U+2060) after any hyphen, slash or dash INSIDE that pair. The nbsp
     alone is not enough and this is the case that proved it: "everything else
     in-between." duly kept "else" with "in-between.", and Safari broke at the HYPHEN
     instead, stranding "between." — the same orphan one word further on.
  3. A 20-CHARACTER CAP, above which the pair is left alone. Not a taste call, the
     measure: an unbreakable run wider than the column has nowhere to go and
     .c-content__summary is `overflow-wrap: normal`, so nothing would catch it. The
     narrowest this standfirst gets is 264px at 21px mono — exactly 20 characters. An
     orphan is cosmetic; text hanging out of its column is a bug.

  Applied per LINE, not per paragraph: a single newline becomes a <br> and each run
  wraps independently, so the last line is not the only one that can strand a word.

  The text is a plain-text CMS field, so each line is escaped here and the only raw
  markup is the <br> we generate ourselves.
#}
{% macro standfirst(text) %}
{%- set out = [] -%}
{%- for line in text|split("\n") -%}
    {#- split(' ') with no filter: consecutive spaces survive the re-join, so the
        author's own spacing comes back untouched. -#}
    {%- set words = line|trim|split(' ') -%}
    {%- set n = words|length -%}
    {#- measured on the PLAIN pair: nbsp and the joiners are zero-width, so counting
        them would make the cap drift with punctuation. -#}
    {%- set plain = n > 1 ? words[n - 2] ~ ' ' ~ words|last : '' -%}
    {%- if n > 1 and plain|length <= 20 -%}
        {%- set head = words|slice(0, n - 2)|join(' ') -%}
        {%- set glued = (words[n - 2] ~ " " ~ words|last)|replace({
            '-': '-⁠', '/': '/⁠', '–': '–⁠', '—': '—⁠'
        }) -%}
        {%- set out = out|merge([((head ? head ~ ' ' : '') ~ glued)|e]) -%}
    {%- else -%}
        {%- set out = out|merge([line|trim|e]) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{{- out|join('<br>')|raw -}}
{% endmacro %}
